# `npx cap add ios` writes this, and it is a build output: an Xcode project
# regenerated from capacitor.config.json and package.json on every machine that
# runs the command. Committing it means merge conflicts in a .pbxproj, which is
# a file nobody can read a diff of.
#
# THE EXCEPTION, AND IT MATTERS: once the entitlement, the bundle id and the
# signing team are set in Xcode they live in ios/App/App/App.entitlements and
# ios/App/App.xcodeproj. Those are not regenerated — they are settings. If this
# is ever built on a second machine, they are set again by hand from README.md,
# which is why README.md lists them rather than assuming the folder survives.
ios/
node_modules/
